image-487"><figcaption>Figure 8</figcaption></figure>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading"><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2>



<p>Hinge crease is one of three types of Origami folds. Although hinge crea=
ses may help determine various polygons positions, their true purpose is so=
mething else. It is a known fact that only the <a href=3D"https://abrashior=
igami.com/ridge-crease/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer noopener">ridg=
e creases</a> are needed in determining the polygon positions during Crease=
 pattern analysis, the flaps mutual orientation, when the model is fully fl=
attened, is determined by the hinge creases alone. And that is its true nat=
ure.</p>
